\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Calibration sweep for the persistence-image (PI) vectorization, one-at-a-time around the default calibration ($q=0.95$, $\alpha =1.05$, $\sigma _{\text  {pixels}}=0.75$, $G=64$; Section~\ref {ssec:calibration}), for both the Thomas and nested-Thomas design distributions (Section~\ref {sec:simulator}). Diagrams use the default $DTM_{\{5,10,15\}}$, $H_0{+}H_1$ pipeline and shared-weight architecture of Section~\ref {ssec:encoder-fusion}. Cells report $\mathcal  {L}$ (Section~\ref {ssec:eval-protocol}, mean $\pm $ sd over 3 seeds). $^\dagger $ marks configurations that diverge on at least one of the three seeds (per-seed $\mathcal  {L} \approx 0.9$--$1.0$, i.e.\ no better than predicting the design-distribution mean); their mean is dominated by the diverged seed(s) and should not be read as a stable estimate.}}{23}{table.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
